// @ens-test
// @exit 0
// @stdout PASS a wait lasts at least as long as the platform promises
// @stdout PASS only Windows is allowed to come short of the count
// @stdout PASS a wait after a wait still lasts as long as the count given
// @stdout PASS a count of zero returns
// @stdout PASS a count below zero returns
// @stdout PASS the clock moves over a wait
// @stdout 6/6 tests passed
// The wait std.thread will block on and the clock that measures it, exercised on the host running
// the suite. Only a floor is asserted, because nothing bounds how long a loaded machine leaves a
// thread waiting. A wait that comes short is what these tests exist to catch.

main() -> int {
    return 0;
}
